    "curricularHighlights": "California Northstate University College of Medicine is committed to delivering an educational experience to ensure the student's goal of becoming a confident and skillful physician. The curriculum at the College of Medicine is based on Clinical Presentations (CPs); symptoms or conditions that cause patients to seek the help of a physician. At the College of Medicine, basic science, clinical knowledge, clinical reasoning, ethics training, hands-on learning of medical skills as well as on research-oriented activities, and participation in patient care at our Sacramento affiliate hospitals and clinics will help our students become patient-centered, confident leaders, and long-term learners in medicine.",
